Mechanism: Because routes are present and adjacencies are stable, packets are forwarded correctly through the leaf–spine–super-spine topology, yielding successful ping tests.

Localization: No device shows interface, protocol, or policy anomalies. All FRR/BGP daemons and links are operating nominally.

Root cause: No active network fault—issue is not reproducible at this time.

Corrective fix: None required for the network. If timeouts persist, check application/service or host firewall/DNS on the endpoints and provide timestamps/ports so we can correlate with fabric telemetry. 
